# A87 TeraDesk (sd-tera, #Z autorun; 640x480). TeraDesk's THEACTIVE is
# (16,0,280,19) (desktop.rsc tree 0 object 2: x 16, w 280 -> x 16..295;
# titles Desk 16..63, File 64..111, View 112..159, Window 160..223,
# Options 224..295). The pointer rests in the bar row RIGHT of Options
# at (400,8) — outside gl_ctwait — clicks there, then the HELP key
# (IKBD 0x62 make / 0xE2 break) is pressed while it still rests there.
# EmuTOS: no hand-over, no track, the click is ctl_pd's and dropped
# (chk_ctrl gl_rmenu), the key reaches TeraDesk at once -> HELP dialog
# (main.c hndlkey -> showhelp). Before the fix TeraDesk was parked in the
# control manager's track until the pointer left the row, so the key was
# processed only after the park (E), not at D. Then Cancel (427,385)
# closes the help dialog, File is hovered (the title track must still
# open File), and a click on the parked pointer cancels it (A73 2b).
200 parkbr
1000 arm
1100 mark A_IDLE
1400 move 400 8
1900 mark B_REST_RIGHT_OF_OPTIONS
2200 down
2203 up
2700 mark C_CLICKED_THERE
3000 key 62
3003 key E2
3600 mark D_HELP_KEY_WHILE_RESTING
4000 parkbr
4700 mark E_PARKED
5000 move 427 385
5300 down
5303 up
5600 parkbr
6200 mark F_HELP_CLOSED
6500 move 88 8
7000 mark G_FILE_TITLE_HOVER
7300 parkbr
7800 down
7803 up
8400 mark H_CLOSED
